      "timestamp_raw": "Dec 9, 2020 17:45:17 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "some new pics of S. moorei bouquet Southern Baldwin Co, AL.  Pics taken early december 2020!   Body of the trap below the \"head\" can sometimes produce a yellow tinge, much like leaves in the fall before they senesce!  Red coloration under the lid becomes more intense as the traps age.    The traps last unusually long: in comparison, my hurricane creek whites are totally brown now!  Cold-dam?  Naw, HAWT-DAYAM!!!<br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/50700439307_2f184cfb79_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/50700362526_fca89b310e_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/50700443857_217b2ab5be_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/50700445587_383891f4b2_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/>",
